interface "ISession"    as I1
interface "IAccess"     as I2
interface "IIntegrity"  as I3
interface "IRisk"       as I4
interface "IAudit"      as I5
interface "IChat"       as I6

AUTH  -up- I1
AC    -up- I2
CUST  -up- I3
RISK  -up- I4
AUD   -up- I5
AI    -up- I6

WEB   ..> I1
WEB   ..> I3
WEB   ..> I4
WEB   ..> I6
CASES ..> I2
EVID  ..> I2
CUST  ..> I2
RISK  ..> I3
AI    ..> I2
AI    ..> I3
AI    ..> I4
AUD   ..> I2

EVID  --> FS
CASES --> DB
EVID  --> DB
CUST  --> DB
RISK  --> DB
AUD   --> DB
AC    --> DB
AI    ..> LLM : <<external call>>

note right of AC
  Every component that reads case-scoped data
  depends on IAccess. One provider, one rule -
  the abstraction introduced in Sprint 4 after
  aggregates were found unscoped.
end note
@enduml
